## Models carried

All four models are paper sheets the student and teacher fill; they grow by stage (the progression's "Model:" lines).
The K to 2 band begins the 2 to 3 stage in grade 2; grade 3 finishes it, and grades 4 and 5 use the 4 to 5 stage.

| Model | Where it comes from | Used here | How it grows |
|---|---|---|---|
| text map | The K to 2 band (k-si-inform, model_out), at the 2 to 3 stage from grade 2 | Units 1 and 5 (grade 3: grouped parts with headings; the facts of a problem); units 10, 11, 15 and 14's model_in (grade 4: a plan's steps; a text's structure with a defined term; facts feeding the opinion); units 20, 21 and 24 (grade 5: two texts side by side; a progress report) | 2 to 3 stage: main idea and details in grouped boxes with headings; 4 to 5 stage: subtopics with a defined term and the text's structure named, two texts side by side in grade 5 |
| story map | The K to 2 band (k-si-narrate, model_out) | Units 2 and 8 (grade 3: beginning, middle and end with a feeling; problem, events, solution with a dialogue line); units 12 and 16 (grade 4: a scene with its theme; a group task in order); units 18 and 25 (grade 5: scenes joined across chapters; a project across days) | 2 to 3 stage: problem, events and solution; 4 to 5 stage: scenes or days with the key moment marked and a reflective ending |
| cause chain | The K to 2 band (k-si-explain, model_out) | Units 2, 4, 5 and 6 (grade 3: a level's decision and its effect; a life cycle and a force); units 13, 15 and 17 (grade 4: energy and erosion; partial products; causes weighed); units 19, 21 and 22 (grade 5: food energy from the sun; causes of the Revolution; decimal steps) | 2 to 3 stage: linked boxes with "so"; 4 to 5 stage: links named with "as a result", "which causes", and one cause marked as mattering more |
| claim chart | The K to 2 band (k-si-argue, model_out) | Units 3, 6 and 7 (grade 3: claim, source and a reason built on; claim with two pieces of evidence; fraction claim with a critique); units 9, 10, 14 and 16 (grade 4: options, evidence and the compromise; claim from two sources; grouped reasons; test results); units 19, 23, 24 and 25 (grade 5: claim from data; reasons linked to points; claim, example, therefore; corroborated sources) | 2 to 3 stage: a claim and two reasons with their sources; 4 to 5 stage: claim, evidence, reasoning and an answer to another claim |

All four go on to grade 6, where the cards beside them come off for levels 3 and 4. Sentence frames and word banks
are scaffolds, not models (progression read 2026-11-21): they are withdrawn on the days in The course in brief.

