hort sources on a made-up town's fight to open its library to all (Curio Class's own, invented for practice) and say whether they agree; argue to the teacher; write a claim from both; then a respond day. The end-of-unit record and the year's sheet go on to grade 6's teacher. Out: the research and the action (social studies) | Last because social studies' civil rights research runs weeks 30 to 32. No course-level check samples it (Course-level checks, Weeks) | Candidate: PRIME Breadth.ELD, argue on history; bar item 13, narrate returns harder | Jim Crow laws, segregation and violence against Black Americans are named plainly, as the host does; no role-play, no "both sides" task on rights. Civil rights struggles of Latino, Asian American and Native peoples are named where the host names them; no student is asked about discrimination they or their family have faced. Home language: corroborar and corroborate are cognates; civiles and civil are cognates, and derechos and rights are not, so the card carries both. Agent reads: sensitivity; spanish |
